    "body": "Exclude `@` characters when detecting `user/repo` style sources while deciding to prepend `https://github.com/`.\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-10-18T10:08:07Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for finding this and making a PR!\r\n\r\nI think it is reasonable to have even more restrictions for which 'user/repo' should be used to infer 'https://github.com/user/repo' source. In particular, only characters which GitHub itself allows to be included in 'user' (alphanumeric and \"-\") and 'repo' (alphanumeric, \"-\", \"_\", \".\").\r\n\r\nThis now should fixed on latest `main` branch.",
